    7.1.2 Sex Composition
    There were more males than females in the population of Ghor, with the males comprising 51.2
    percent of the total population. The sex ratio recorded for the province in September 2012 was 105
    males for every 100 females, which is a little lower than the sex ratio on record for the whole country
    as reported in the National Risk and Vulnerability Assessment Survey 2011-2012 (Afghanistan Living
    Conditions Survey) which was 106 males for every 100 females.

